- 2)` holds, the radius bound is satisfied. This occurs when `(Finset.univ \\ ballWithin G 1 u).card ≤ W - 2`. Vertices outside `ballWithin G 1 u` have specific constraints on their weights and adjacencies.\n\nThe size of the set of vertices outside the 1-ball around *u* needs investigation, as this is directly related to the weight *W*. Large sets of vertices not adjacent to *u* imply other centers are needed which increase *W*. Every center *z* contributes to *W*.\n\nEach center *z* gives an additional 2 to *W*. If there are *p* centers in *V2*, then *W* is at least `2p + |V1|`. All vertices in *V0* are dominated by the *p* centers; thus, the size of *V0* is bounded by the sum of neighborhood sizes of the centers.\n\n\n**Evaluating Ball Coverage & Contradiction**\n\nConsidering whether a 1-step ball from a center covers enough vertices and exploring the 2-step ball case instead. Examining elements contained within `ballWithin G 2 u`. If another center *z* is adjacent to *u*, the 1-ball around *z* is contained in the 2-ball around *u*. Considering alternatives to proving `prove_e20263a9`.\n\n**Assessing Theorem Direction and Dependencies**\n\nInvestigating the possibility of proving the negation of the candidate theorem `refute_e20263a9`. Recognizing that this is not possible because the candidate is true. The goal is now focused on proving `prove_e20263a9`. Identifying that the previous rejection was due to the remaining use of `sorryAx` in both theorems.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport os, glob\n\nmathlib_path = '/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph'\nfiles = glob.glob(mathlib_path + '/**/*.lean', recursive=True)\nprint('Found SimpleGraph files:', len(files))\nfor f in files:\n    if any(w in os.path.basename(f).lower() for w in ['metric', 'dist', 'conn', 'path', 'walk']):\n        print(f)\n\"","Cwd":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/