*W*. Consequently, the eccentricity of any vertex *v* is at least *W*, leading to `ballWithin G (W - 1) v` not covering the entire vertex set. Applying the `ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge` theorem, the cardinality of `ballWithin G (W-1) v` must be at least *W*.\n\nFocusing on the set *V2* (vertices with value 2 under *f*), every vertex in *V0* (value 0 under *f*) is adjacent to a vertex in *V2*. Hence, the union of *V0* and *V2* is a subset of the union of `ballWithin G 1 z` for all *z* in *V2*.\n\nThe size of *V0* union *V2* is calculated as `|V| - W + 2|V2|`. Exploring relationships between distances of sets of vertices with specific assignments in Roman Domination.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/scratch_rdn.lean","ContentOffset":0,"EndLine":100,"StartLine":1,"toolAction":"View scratch_rdn.lean","toolSummary":"View scratch_rdn.lean"}}]}
